  "description": "Evaluate ranking precision and recall trajectories across classification thresholds and compute Average Precision.\n\nUnlike ROC curves which can present misleadingly optimistic scores under heavy negative class imbalance, PR curves accurately reflect detection quality.\n\n### Mathematical Formulation\n$$\n\\text{AP} = \\sum_{k=1}^N (R_k - R_{k-1}) P_k, \\quad P_k = \\frac{\\text{TP}_k}{\\text{TP}_k + \\text{FP}_k}\n$$\n\n### Step-by-Step Implementation\n1. Sort binary ground truth targets in descending order of predicted confidence scores\n2. Compute cumulative true positives TP and false positives FP at each rank\n3. Evaluate precision and recall arrays and compute Average Precision area\n\n### Returns\nDictionary with 'precision', 'recall', and 'average_precision'.",
  "theory": "## Understanding the Theory: Precision-Recall Curve & Average Precision\n\n### Core Intuition: Why Do We Need This?\nIn computational mathematics and machine learning, robust algorithmic routines ensure calculations are both mathematically sound and computationally efficient. **Precision-Recall Curve & Average Precision** implements a core computational building block.\n\nUnlike ROC curves which can present misleadingly optimistic scores under heavy negative class imbalance, PR curves accurately reflect detection quality. In this problem, the goal is to: evaluate ranking precision and recall trajectories across classification thresholds and compute average precision.\n\n### Mathematical Principles & Formulation\nThe core governing equation for this operation is:\n\n$$\n\\text{AP} = \\sum_{k=1}^N (R_k - R_{k-1}) P_k, \\quad P_k = \\frac{\\text{TP}_k}{\\text{TP}_k + \\text{FP}_k}\n$$\n\nEvery term in this formulation plays a precise mathematical role in ensuring dimensional consistency, numerical stability, and correct algorithmic behavior.\n\n### Step-by-Step Computational Workflow\n1. **Phase 1**: Sort binary ground truth targets in descending order of predicted confidence scores\n2. **Phase 2**: Compute cumulative true positives TP and false positives FP at each rank\n3. **Phase 3**: Evaluate precision and recall arrays and compute Average Precision area\n\n### Practical Machine Learning Applications & Nuances\n* **Algorithmic Complexity**: Designing routines with optimal time and space complexity ensures they scale gracefully to large datasets.\n* **Numerical Accuracy**: Safeguarding calculations against floating-point underflow or division by zero ensures consistent results.\n* **Vectorization**: Implementing operations with contiguous array buffers avoids interpreter overhead.",
  "examples": [
    "Input: y_true = [1, 1, 0, 1], y_scores = [0.9, 0.8, 0.7, 0.4]\n\nOutput: {\"precision\": [1.0, 1.0, 0.6667, 0.75], \"recall\": [0.3333, 0.6667, 0.6667, 1.0], \"average_precision\": 0.9167}\n\nExplanation: Evaluated ml_precision_recall_ap under standard test conditions."
