  "starterCode": "import numpy as np\n\ndef ml_precision_recall_ap(y_true: list, y_scores: list) -> dict:\n    pass",
  "solution": "### 💡 Intuition & Approach\nThe implementation computes **Precision-Recall Curve & Average Precision** by following direct mathematical principles, leveraging vectorized operations to ensure both correctness and optimal runtime efficiency.\n\n### ⚡ Python Reference Implementation\n```python\nimport numpy as np\n\ndef ml_precision_recall_ap(y_true: list, y_scores: list) -> dict:\n    t, s = np.array(y_true), np.array(y_scores)\n    idx = np.argsort(s)[::-1]\n    ts = t[idx]\n    tp = np.cumsum(ts == 1); fp = np.cumsum(ts == 0)\n    prec = tp / (tp + fp); rec = tp / max(1, np.sum(t == 1))\n    ap = np.sum((rec - np.concatenate([[0], rec[:-1]])) * prec)\n    return {'precision': np.round(prec, 4).tolist(), 'recall': np.round(rec, 4).tolist(), 'average_precision': round(float(ap), 4)}\n```\n\n### ⏱️ Complexity Analysis\n- **Time Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ where $N$ represents the size of the primary input.\n- **Space Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ auxiliary memory for computing and storing output representations.",
